<title>EGYPT: Egypt sends supplies for Sudanese flood victims.</title>
<headline>Egypt sends supplies for Sudanese flood victims.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>An EgyptAir Boeing 707 cargo plane left Cairo for Khartoum on Sunday with 40 tonnes of food, tents, blankets and medical supplies donated by the Egyptian government to victims of Nile floods, Cairo airport officials said.</p>
<p>Floods have destroyed more than 2,600 houses in Khartoum province, a Sudanese newspaper reported on Friday.</p>
<p>The privately owned daily Akhbar al-Youm said floods swept away 2,618 houses in the southern Jebel Aulia area and at least 4,000 people were stranded there without shelter.</p>
